<title>AUSTRALIA: KINETIC POWER LIST AT 15 PERCENT PREMIUM.</title>
<headline>KINETIC POWER LIST AT 15 PERCENT PREMIUM.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in industrial battery manufacturer Kinetic Power Ltd made their debut on the Australian Stock Exchange at A$1.15 on Thursday, a 15 percent premium to their A$1.00 issue price.</p>
<p>The issue of 16 million shares, underwritten by PG Intercapital Ltd, raised A$16 million.</p>
<p>By 2.50 p.m. (0450 GMT), Kinetic power shares were at A$1.21, 21 cents above their issue price after touching a high of A$1.22 and a low of A$1.14. Turnover was 1.3 million shares.</p>
<p>--Walter Watson, Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1810</p>
